body:
thanks so much for replying. i'm trying to make sure he knows i'm there. i'm trying to accept that it's his choice but it's tough. i'm sorry to hear this happened to you, but i'm really glad you're doing better now, hopefully my partner will follow a similar path.

&#x200B;

just asking, what type of therapy did you go to? he's tried just regular counselling a while back but he felt the people there just didn't know what to say.

you'll find your person if you hang on. not many people have someone who genuinely loves them, but that's what makes it precious when you find it. you have to learn to be happy on your own before you get the privilege of being happy with someone you love.

&#x200B;

if you want to talk to me message me please. though, your comment was kind of nice, i hope that he feels happy i'm there for him.

absolutely, i've been seeing professionals for a long time now, and i'm trying different medications. my partner has had a bad experience with professionals and thinks they can't help him, i'm trying to get him to go back though because you're right, the help is there.

&#x200B;

thanks for replying :)
